    {
      "column_index": 1,
      "header_id": "C13",
      "x_range": [
        473.5,
        2200.0
      ],
      "section_title": "Attractor Logic: One of Grasshopper's most powerful parametric strategies.",
      "section_number": 1,
      "teaching_text": "1- Attractor Logic: One of Grasshopper's most powerful parametric strategies.\r\n\r\n- Attractor Logic is a very simple design concept based on distances. However the results could become amazing.\r\n\r\n- We will build a simple parametric definition below and understand how attractors work in Grasshopper.\r\n\r\n- Build a squarish grid of points: S 10, Ex 10, Ey 10.\r\n\r\n- Construct a Point and keep in without any INPUTS.\r\n\r\n- Use a \"Move\" component and feed in the Point. Use an MD Slider to feed to direction.\r\n\r\n- Change the MD Slider's domains to 100 in both X & Y.\r\n\r\n- Get the Points from the Squarish grid and flatten them\r\n\r\n- Get the Ditances between the flattened points of the squarish grid and the moved point.\r\n\r\n- Check out the distances using a panel.\r\n\r\n- Find the minimum & maximum of all distances by using the \"Bounds\" component.\r\n\r\n- Use a \"Vector 2Pt\" component:\r\n1t Point Input = Constructed Point\r\n1st Point Input = All Points of the squarish grid\r\n\r\n- Move all the points of the squarish grid by using the \"Vector 2Pt\" as translation vectors.\r\n\r\n- Make Lines between the points of the squarish grid and the newly moved ones.\r\n\r\n- The Lines represent the \"Attraction\" between the constructed point and the squarish grid points.\r\n\r\n- Find below numerous examples of how to affect this attraction effect, by:\r\n- Manipulating vector lengths with commands, such as multiplication.\r\n- Remapping data.",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C296",
      "additional_teaching_panels": [],
      "sub_annotations": [],
      "concepts_taught": [
        "Construct a Point and keep in without any INPUTS.",
        "Move",
        "Check out the distances using a panel.",
        "Bounds",
        "Use a \"Vector 2Pt\" component:",
        "Vector 2Pt",
        "Attraction",
        "Remapping data."
      ],
