    {
      "column_index": 7,
      "header_id": "C38",
      "x_range": [
        12044.9,
        12945.6
      ],
      "section_title": "Paneling: Practical Example",
      "section_number": 7,
      "teaching_text": "7- Paneling: Practical Example\r\n\r\nLet us use the result from the previous definition to make interesting panelization options:\r\n\r\n\r\nA- Manipulating Faces\r\n\r\n1- Extrude all faces in the Z direction\r\n\r\n2- Extrude / Offset all faces Normal to Surface.\r\n\r\n\r\nB- Manipualting Edges:\r\n\r\nZ direction:\r\n\r\n1- Move one edge of the panels in the Z direction.\r\n\r\n2- Loft the moved edges with their respective facing edges.\r\n\r\nNormal to Surface:\r\n\r\n3- Repeat step (1) but now the edges being moved Normal to the surface.\r\n\r\n4- Loft the moved edges with their respective facing edges.",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C299",
