    {
      "column_index": 9,
      "header_id": "C271",
      "x_range": [
        15541.6,
        15917.1
      ],
      "section_title": "Geometry Morphing",
      "section_number": 8,
      "teaching_text": "8- Geometry Morphing:\r\n\r\nAnother powerful way of panelization is to morph geometry onto a panelized surface, with a customized base shape.\r\n\r\nWe will use the previous definition and morph a modeled geometry in Rhino.\r\n\r\n- First, reference the modeled geometry in Rhino in a \"Geometry\" component.\r\n\r\n- Use a \"Bounding Box\" and plug in the referenced geometry in the C INPUT.\r\n\r\n- Use a \"Surface Box\" and plug in:\r\n1- Base surface in S INPUT.\r\n2- Divide Domain² OUTPUT in D INPUT.\r\n3- Number in H INPUT.\r\n\r\n- Use a \"Box Morph\" and plug in:\r\n1- Referenced geometry in G INPUT.\r\n2- The first B OUTPUT from \"Bounding Box\" in R INPUT.\r\n3- OUTPUT of \"Surface Box\" in T INPUT.\r\n\r\n- Note that you can always change the referenced geometry and then reference it again, and the final result will update accordingly.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT:\r\n\r\n- If, for any reason, you would need to construct a non-regular surface division (without Domain Division), then you would need to construct Twisted Boxs without using the \"Surface Box\".\r\n\r\nFor this purpose, you will use the parameters of that non-regular surface divisions and use the \"Twisted Box\" component to generate Twisted Boxes, which can then be used for the T INPUT of the \"Box Morph\".",
      "teaching_panel_id": "C298",
      "additional_teaching_panels": [
        {
          "id": "C224",
          "text": "WARNING\r\n\r\nThe operations on the right side are heavy and may crash your GH file.\r\n\r\nPlease enable and disable components while trying them, so that not all of them would be running simultaneously.\r\n\r\nTry to disable all components on the right side, except for the ones needed to run the components.\r\n\r\nAlso, try to Lock Solver if needed by Right-Clicking anywhere and selecting \"Lock Solver\""
        }
      ],
