      "section_title": "Exercise: Sun Orientation",
      "section_number": 9,
      "teaching_text": "9- Exercise: Sun Orientation\r\n\r\nStart with preparing the geometries:\r\n\r\n1- Place a Point to represent the sun Position\r\n2- Construct a Surface and divide it to get sub-surfaces\r\n3- Evaluate the sub-surfaces in order to extract the points and their respective normal vectors\r\n\r\nOrientation Method 1:  Using the \"Orient\" component\r\n\r\n1- Build Vectors between each of the sub-surfaces and the sun point (Using Vector 2Pt)\r\n2- Build planes normal to the vectors\r\n3- Orient the sub-surfaces according the planes normal to the vectors\r\n\r\nOrientation Method 2: Using the \"Orient Direction\" component\r\n\r\n1- Build Vectors between each of the sub-surfaces and the sun point\r\n2- Adjust amplitude of the vectors to match the original vector lengths\r\n>> These would be used for the Direction B input of the component\r\n3- Use the Centroids of the sub-surfaces as Point A and Point B\r\n4- Direction A: Original normal vectors of the sub-surfaces",
